  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for `NRS_484B_440_1_o3` on the second of six runs. It reported 5 witnesses, 8 names, no compositions and one narrowing that I declared.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_440_1_o3.lean`):\n- **Class:** `x` is in `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** all of these hold:\n  - `x` is halted (speed at or below `p.speed_resolution`).\n  - `x` is on a highway and on its roadway.\n  - The place is not inside a business or residence district.\n  - `x` is not disabled. Following the node, disabled is read as engine off, hazard lamps on and `x` on the roadway.\n- **Duty:** on every roadway `x` occupies on that highway, the sight distance is at least 200 ft.\n\n**The choice I made:** the node says \"the sight distance at x's place\" but doesn't say which region that is. I read it from the roadway `x` is on, and if `x` straddles more than one roadway, each must meet 200 ft. This is recorded as a narrowing on span g12, so later sessions will see it.\n\n**Witnesses:** the test scene is a rural highway 400 m long. Its roadway's sight distance is 30 m (below 200 ft, which is 60.96 m) or 300 m. The first gate run failed to build because I gave region ids as text when they must be numbers; that was the only fix needed.\n\n| Scenario | Expected | Scene |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | violated | Vehicle halted, sight distance 30 m |\n| permit | compliant | Vehicle halted, sight distance 300 m |\n| idle | not applicable | Vehicle moving at 15 m/s |\n| blind | unknown | As forbid, with the sight distance hidden from the source |\n| branch_1 | not applicable | As forbid, but engine off and hazard lamps on |\n\nI didn't find anything wrong with the node, so there is no defect to report. The run log and choices are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
